      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T16:18:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "btif_config_get_bin() will modify return len only if len of config value is smaller than input len.\n```\n*length \u003d std::min(value_vec-\u003esize(), *length);\n```\nIn our case, if config value is 060199, len is 3 byte, the condition will still pass.\nI will keep using btif_config_get_bin_length here.\n\n\n\n\n\nThere will be a error using static_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e instead of (unit8_t*)\n```\nStatic_cast from \u0027uint16_t *\u0027 (aka \u0027unsigned short *\u0027) to \u0027uint8_t *\u0027 (aka \u0027unsigned char *\u0027) is not allowed\n```\nI tried using reinterpret_cast and it will pass.\nFrom above statuc_cast article, I think I will keep using C-style cast right now.",
      "parentUuid": "0d6afc1c_c4589210",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1289,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1289,
        "endChar": 59
